This Terraform program creates a VPC with two private subnets, an EFS file system, and two EC2 instances in the private subnets, mounting the EFS file system for shared storage. The EC2 instances are configured with basic user data to mount the EFS file system. The `instance_type` variable has a default value of `t3.micro`, which can be changed to any valid AWS instance type. The `key_name` variable is set to `my-key-pair`, which should be replaced with the actual name of your SSH key pair. The `security_groups` variable is set to `["sg-0abcdef1234567890"]`, which should be replaced with the actual ID of your security group.

